@{
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
    ViewBag.Title = "Part8 - Grid, Column and Cell Options";
}
<div class="col-sm-12">
    <p>This tutorial shows you how can you customize many things of Grid, Column, and Cell Options.</p>

    <h4>1. Merging: Fanex.Grid support merge cell of columns and cell of rows.</h4>

    <ul>
        <li>
            Merge cells of columns, we declare <text class="text-danger">"MergeColNumber" </text> property in column, and set this property to "n" (n is a number). After this column, we must not declare "n" column(s) next. We can treat this property like "colspan" element  of "td" in table
        </li>
        <li>
            Merge cells of rows, we declare <text class="text-danger">"MergeRowNumber" </text> property in column,  and set this property to "n" (n is a number). After this row, we must not declare this column in "n" rows next. We can treat this property like "rowspan" element of "td" in table.
        </li>
        <li>We can see example at Merging</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>2. Format Number/ Date:</h4>
    <ul>
        <li>
            We can format number value in cell by declaring <text class="text-danger">"FormatNumber"</text> in "columns", see http://numeraljs.com/ for more format types.
        </li>
        <li>We can also format positive and negative value in cell by declaring <text class="text-danger">"FormatPositive" and "FormatNegative" </text>, in this format ‘$’ character is value, and other things around is decoration things.</li>
        <li>We format Date Time by declaring <text class="text-danger">"FormatDateTime"</text> property in column, see http://momentjs.com/ for more format types.</li>
        <li>We can see example below for more detail:</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Gird Option:</p>

    <pre class="brush: javascript">
        var gridOptions =
        {
            columns: [
                { HeaderText: "Header 1", Width: 60, Name: "No", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "center" },
                { HeaderText: "Header 2", Width: 70, Name: "Text1", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "right", FormatNumber: "0,0.00", FormatNegative: '($)' },
                { HeaderText: "Header 3", Width: 200, Name: "Number1", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "right", FormatDateTime: "MMMM Do YYYY" },
                { HeaderText: "Header 4", Width: 100, Name: "Number2", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "right", FormatNumber: "0,0." },
                { HeaderText: "Header 5", Width: 160, Name: "Number3", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "right", FormatNumber: "0,0.0" },
                { HeaderText: "Header 6", Width: 110, Name: "Text2" },
                { HeaderText: "Header 7", Width: 120, Name: "Text3" },
                { HeaderText: "Header 8", Width: 150, Name: "Text4" },
                { HeaderText: "Header 9", Width: 90, Name: "Number4", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "right", FormatNumber: "0,0.00" },
                { HeaderText: "Header 10", Width: 120, Name: "Number5", HeaderAlign: "center", CellAlign: "right", FormatNumber: "0,0.00", FormatPositive: '[$]' }
            ],
            bodyRows: generateDataTime(100),
            gridExpandHeight: 150
        };
    </pre>

    <p>Result is: </p>

    <img width="100%" src="~/Content/Images/Part9Example1.png" />

    <h4>3. Show/Hide Column:</h4>
    <ul>
        <li>By default, we can set hide columns in Grid Option by specific two properties: <text class="text-danger">"showColumnsShowHide" set to "false" </text> and <text class="text-danger">"columnsNeedHide" set to an array contains all index We need hide </text> , example when we need hide column 0, 4, 5 so we will set that property to [0,4,5].</li>
        <li>
            <ul>
                <text class="text-danger">
                    The other way, we can show/hide columns after Grid rendered
                </text>, by this way:
                <li>$("#gridId").fanexGrid("hideColumns", gridOptions, [0, 1, 3, 7]); for hide columns</li>
                <li>or $("#gridId").fanexGrid("hideColumns", gridOptions, []); for show all columns.</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li>Here is example hide 3,4,5,6,10</li>
    </ul>

    <img width="100%" src="~/Content/Images/Part9Example2.png" />

    <h4>4. Fanex.Grid support a large of properties allow us customize cell easily.</h4>
    <p>See Fanex.Grid Api for more information.</p>

    <h4>5. Append Body Rows after Gird rendered</h4>
    <p>We still can add rows to body by function below:</p>

    <pre class="brush: javascript">
        $("#gridId").fanexGrid('appendBody',gridOptions, GenerateNormalData(10));
    </pre>

    <h4>6. Auto Truncate</h4>
    <p>
        In some cases, we need to hide data when it exceed column width, sometimes we want it to drop new line, this case  was supported by default. Sometimes, we need data exceeded hidden. For hidden case, <text class="text-danger">
    we just specific "allowTruncate" property and set it to true.</text>
    We can see example below:
</p>

    <img width="100%" src="~/Content/Images/Part9Example3.png" />

    <h4>7. Others Gird Options</h4>

    <p>See Fanex.Grid Api for more information.</p>
</div>
